    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] Born Alan Ernest Caldwell in Liverpool, Storm was the singer and leader of Rory Storm and the Hurricanes, a Liverpudlian band who were contemporaries of the Beatles in the late 1950s and early 1960s.\n[2] Ringo Starr was the drummer for the Hurricanes before joining the Beatles in August 1962, replacing original drummer Pete Best.\n[3] He fronted his own eponymous band, known as the Keef Hartley Band or Keef Hartley's Big Band, and played at Woodstock.\n[4] \"You and Me (Babe)\" is a song by English musician Ringo Starr, released as the final track on his 1973 album \"Ringo\"."
